Hmm, judging only from the description, I don't buy it.
All of the things should be able to be implemented with normal
spinlocks.  If not, the design is very likely wrong.

> I also think that the group lock might be acquired uselessly in many cases.

Yes.  We basically think of a single lock in all pcm_lib.c operations.
This is the cause of the whole problems.  If we think of only a single
lock, it should be really a single lock.  If we need more finer locks,
we need two kind of locks in PCM operations themselves.


